WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.934
22 days.

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.369
That's how much longer

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.303
beauty salons

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.405
are able to stay open in Afghanistan

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.140
under Taliban rule.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.241
All shops across

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.175
the country were given

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.877
one month's notice to close down.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:13.446
That is according to a Taliban spokesman.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.782
It is the latest move by the Taliban

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.350
to roll back rights for women

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.352
who are already largely

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.453
confined to their homes

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.856
with bans on this work and study.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:26.126
Here's Katy Polglase with more

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.396
Driving through the streets of Kabul,

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.364
among the brightly colored shops

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:31.765
is one

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.932
lost symbol of women

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.602
being visible in the public life,

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.270
squeezing them out of sight.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.471
Taliban authorities

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.606
ordered beauty parlors

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.541
to be shut within the month,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.575
sending shockwaves

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.744
for women already gripped in a chokehold.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.546
A salon owner

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.114
who did not want to be identified

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.382
for safety reasons

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.384
told CNN the Taliban's order

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.453
means her poverty stricken family

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.288
cannot afford the bare essentials

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:57.290
I don't

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.324
understand why beauty

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.360
salons should be banned, she says.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.961
My husband is jobless

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:02.962
and this beauty salon

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.265
is the only means to feed my family.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.734
I, for kids, they need food and clothes.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.002
The Taliban

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.003
seized back power

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.539
in the summer of 20, 21,

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.340
with thousands of terrified families

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.408
flocking to Kabul.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.142
Airport

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.210
desperate to escape

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.179
the group's barbaric rule.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.847
While the Taliban vowed reform,

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.482
promising to be more progressive

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.850
than their previous rule.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.317
Women

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:28.054
were quickly erased from public life,

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.888
banning teenage

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.023
girls from secondary

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.891
and higher education,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.027
and ordering nonprofit organizations

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.762
to stop their female employees

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.230
from coming to work.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:37.931
The salon owner

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:38.898
we spoke to says

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.632
she doesn't know

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.468
what more can be taken from them

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:44.170
before there's nothing left at all.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.872
No woman is showing off her face

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.273
with makeup outside

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.175
and were already wearing hijab in public,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.076
she says.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.678
This will further deprive women of

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.012
their rights and freedoms

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.649
As the Taliban

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.518
slowly chipped away at their rights.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.753
Hope is slowly dwindling for some women,

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.556
but others still haven't been deterred

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.258
from raising their voices,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.560
even if it means risking their lives.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.363
Katie Polglase, CNN, London.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:11.698
All right.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.299
Let's get a deeper understanding

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.834
of the implications of the move.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.535
Joining me now

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.103
in the studio is Fawzia Koofi,

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.605
the former deputy speaker

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:19.939
of the Afghan parliament.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:20.540
Fawzia, great

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.142
to have you here on the show.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.909
Look, I think

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.644
what one of the ladies said there,

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.113
what more can be taken from us?

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:27.914
And just watching that,

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.216
that's moved you, hasn't it?

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.684
It is very emotional

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.987
while we try to demonstrate

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.989
our warrior side, not as a victim,

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.558
but looking at what has been achieved

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.226
over the last 20 years

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.529
and how much women were in the forefront

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.830
of all of that

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.498
fighting for the global security

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.333
and see that now they are kind of

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.735
pushed to corner

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.802
to become invisible

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.238
and erased from all spheres of life is

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.807
is not a very easy moment for me

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.342
who have been part of all ups

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.544
and downs of Afghanistan

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:58.144
Give our viewers

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.879
a sense of some of the stories

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.480
you've been hearing

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.081
because you know, our reporter

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.383
Katie put into context

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.651
in terms of slowly

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.419
chipping away at women's rights,

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.921
slowly pushing away

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.190
women away from civil society.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.125
What are you hearing from Afghan women?

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:13.693
Women of

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.327
Afghanistan are

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.728
very, very disappointed,

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:16.863
obviously

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.664
undergoing a lot

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.065
of mental health pressure

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.267
because can you imagine

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.735
that they are being deprived

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.871
of all the basic fundamental rights,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.273
the right to work education,

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.210
attending gyms, attending parks,

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.046
going to public places,

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.214
and their existence

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.782
and being is being questioned.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.684
Sometimes my colleagues and staff

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:41.521
and like my friends from Kabul,

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.355
tell me that you know,

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.457
when they get out of their homes,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.658
they stop them and tell them

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.693
that you're not supposed

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.228
to go to university or school.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.495
You're not supposed to go to office

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.129
and work.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.864
Why are you out in the street

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.933
that feeling of being controlled

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.968
by somebody

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.003
as a human being is not a nice feeling.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:00.173
The whole existence of being as a woman

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.007
is being now

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.743
kind of taken away from by Taliban.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.846
And I imagine, you know, the salons

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:07.714
and it probably doesn't

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:08.615
mean much

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:09.749
to us here in the West

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.783
who take it for granted,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.085
but for some of these women,

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.486
this was a sanctuary

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.354
when everything else

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.288
is being taken away from.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.523
This is where women could actually speak

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.091
with each other,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.192
spend time with each other.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:21.394
I suspect Exactly.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.595
So these beauty salons were

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.697
not only as a growing business

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.267
because women lost jobs in other fields

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.668
and other areas.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.803
This was a growing business for them,

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.072
but also a place where women could go

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:33.873
and exercise

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:34.540
their feminine

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.010
kind of part of their themselves

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.279
and talk to each other. Social gathering.

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.747
This was probably the only place where

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.448
women could go without being questioned.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.483
Where are they going?

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.318
But now they have asked them to stop

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:45.852
that.

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.087
We are very much disappointed for

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.622
the fact that when these attacks

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.323
come only

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.391
that is the time that women

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:53.760
of Afghanistan news gets to the headlines

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.295
and the world talks about it

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.964
otherwise, about the centuries

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.499
and decades

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.901
worst human rights, a catastrophe.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:02.702
The world doesn't

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.103
really talk a lot about it.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:04.904
And it's as if it's

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.472
one of the forgotten stories.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.174
And this is the disappointing part

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.375
because you know,

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:10.243
we believe that

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.844
what is happening in Afghanistan

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.479
could have a global consequence.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.014
Why do you think is being forgotten?

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.316
The women of Afghanistan

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.417
have been forgotten.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.017
I think the whole

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.218
people of Kabul failing.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.521
Who is failing? The women? The world.

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.189
The world is failing

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:23.923
the women of Afghanistan

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.525
because during the negotiation

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.327
that the Americans had with the Taliban,

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:27.827
the Taliban

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:28.861
clearly said

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.929
and during the negotiation

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:30.930
they had with us,

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.165
I was talking with them.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.866
They clearly said that they will respect

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.168
women, Islamic rights,

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:37.036
that they will allow women to go to work

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.071
and even become prime

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.539
minister and foreign minister.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:40.640
This is something they have said

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.474
during negotiation

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.542
to get the deal signed

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.509
with the Americans.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.944
Once they signed the deal

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.245
and they got to power,

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.580
this is what was given to them.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.681
Basically, Now,

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:49.749
they started slowly

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:51.718
and gradually suppressing women.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:53.019
They started from allowing

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:54.654
not allowing women to go to school,

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.622
which has no space in Islam,

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.691
has no space in other Muslim countries.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.492
And I think this is

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:00.493
where the Muslim countries

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:01.828
really should speak up.

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:02.495
And then the world

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.130
should have a united position

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.431
because the women of Afghanistan

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.432
surely must not become

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.368
a politicized issue. Absolutely.

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.036
Let me ask you this,

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:12.372
Luba Siraj, the the activist

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.906
and the nominee for the Nobel Peace

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.342
Prize has said there's no choice

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.711
but to talk to Afghanistan's new rule

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:19.545
as the time has come,

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.581
she said, to engage with the Taliban.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:23.583
What do you make of that?

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:24.517
Well, so the point is,

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.651
the world has been engaged

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.253
for more than two years with Taliban.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.354
They have been engaged for many,

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.623
many years to get the deal signed,

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.925
which they give so much to the Taliban

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.560
in the whole Doha agreement.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.762
There is no mention of women

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.463
and human rights

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:40.566
This deal is basically a submissive deal

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.667
to the Taliban.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.569
And since they came to power,

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.871
there has been engagement

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:45.905
at different level

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.240
with different levels of Taliban

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:47.840
from the world,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.075
from international community.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.309
Now, the question is,

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:51.611
what have we achieved?

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.079
So I'm not saying we should not engage,

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:54.814
because obviously at the end of any war,

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:55.681
there should be a peace

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.016
and there should be engagement.

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:57.750
What I'm saying is

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.719
there should be a principled engagement

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.954
as a result of which we know what is

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.756
what is it that the world want to engage

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.590
with Taliban.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.392
You know, the further engagement

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:08.294
without any principled position

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:09.862
will only embolden them.

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:11.130
And emboldening of Taliban

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.765
is not in the interests of the country

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:13.499
and in the interests

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.667
of the women of Afghanistan

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.902
and might give them a free pass

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.103
diplomatic legitimacy.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.504
These are all concerns. No. One,

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:20.807
I suspect, at this stage.

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:22.475
Fawzia Koofi, really appreciate you

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:23.576
taking the time to speak to us.

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:24.377
Thank you very much.

